{"title":"2018 OIM Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer. For a permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de9d2e8a7b59a6ffa5d7815742f89c5deb5c0851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots , a_n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"13\" /> of the numbers\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d1c29787cde5e3d40ce09ee0c8cc4f72509f57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, \\cdots , n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" /> we define\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d1f10d232e893e11966d20e243a5a8c7adf7e67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b_k=\\underset{1\\le i\\le k}{min}a_i+\\underset{1\\le j\\le k}{max}a_j\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p>for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc23c6274e3923db68989582e8cefa94237743a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, 2, \\cdots , n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />. We say that the permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de9d2e8a7b59a6ffa5d7815742f89c5deb5c0851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots , a_n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"13\" />, is \"<i>guadian</i>\" if the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd74ae3a40d18a5650872c5cd0a8cd7db777593b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, \\cdots , b_n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />, does not have two equal consecutive elements. How many <i>guadian</i> permutations exsit?\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2018_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OIM_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"OIM Problems and Solutions\">OIM Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017170823\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 51/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1347/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.125      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    6.125      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key w